//! # Knowledge & Technology System
//!
//! This module implements the research and technology progression system for the colony.
//! Unlike traditional "Tech Trees", the system in SCALE is based on a **Data Economy**.
//!
//! ## Core Concepts
//!
//! ### 1. Knowledge (Currency)
//! *   Generated by Pops working at a [`Library`].
//! *   Stored in [`ColonyResources`](crate::layer1::resources::ColonyResources).
//! *   Used to "buy" new technologies via [`unlock_tech`].
//!
//! ### 2. Data Capacity (Limit)
//! *   Every active technology consumes **Data Storage** (measured in TB).
//! *   Capacity is provided by [`BuildingType::ServerBank`](crate::layer1::building::BuildingType::ServerBank)
//!     and the [`BuildingType::Lander`](crate::layer1::building::BuildingType::Lander).
//! *   If `Used Capacity > Total Capacity`, the system enters a **Corruption** state.
//!
//! ### 3. Corruption
//! *   When capacity is exceeded, the system automatically "corrupts" (disables) the most expensive technologies
//!     to free up space.
//! *   Corrupted techs provide no benefits until capacity is restored and they are auto-repaired.
//! *   This creates a "Soft Cap" on tech progress—you can research everything, but you can't *use*
//!     everything simultaneously without massive server infrastructure.
//!
//! ### 4. Memetic Hazards
//! *   Some technologies (like `Tech::VoidWhispers`) are **Hazardous**.
//! *   Researching them triggers an immediate infection event (see [`crate::layer1::memetics`]).
//! *   This represents the danger of uncovering "Forbidden Knowledge".

